   "source": {
    "label": "lem::pb_ind_sg",
    "number": "Lemma 4",
    "quote": "Let $\\cF$ be the family of $1$-sub-Gaussian distributions with means in $\\cR=[\\mu_0^-, \\mu_0^+] \\subset \\R$, and consider MED implemented with $D: (F, \\mu_1) \\mapsto \\frac{(\\mu_1-\\mu_F)^2}{2}\\ind(\\mu_1\\geq \\mu_F)$ and a non-negative and non-increasing sequence $(a_n)_{n \\in \\N}$. Then ... \\[ \\cR_T \\lesssim  K^\\frac{1}{4}T^\\frac{3}{4} \\wedge \\sqrt{KT\\times (\\log(K)+a_T^{-1})} \\;. \\]"
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Proposition 1 extends this same bound to MED with any divergence satisfying Assumption 4 and alpha_n=1; not recorded separately. Range R hidden in constants."
